The pad log (RecordCommunication) reaches disk only when its 1000-line memo fills, so a press during the 18:10 run is not visible.
PadInterface_St02.cpp ProcessReceiceData: right after S=SubString(6,2), a packet whose type is not "90" (lamp status echo) --
key input "00", version "20", anything unknown -- is passed to g_W906PadNote (defined at end of file, 0 in ctests); tools/wb_serve.cpp
W906_OpLogInit points it at W906_OpPadNote = OpLine("PADKEY", packet). HOME = t050400000020; no PADKEY line = the pad sent nothing.
Same lines + end of file. St02_PadInterface, ScanKeyGolden passed; Debug and release wb_serve linked (EastSun's program closed).
Backups D:\HT9045\_review\*.bak_padnote_20261007_181250. WORKLOG row 174.

